(Functional Burden and Systemic Mental Health Effects in Preadolescents Receiving Guided) Tj
T*
(Online Behavioral Therapy for Anxiety: Secondary Analysis from a Two-Year Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(While primary anxiety symptom reduction is important, understanding broader functional and) Tj
T*
(psychological outcomes is essential for clinical decision-making. In our 465-participant) Tj
T*
(trial of internet-delivered therapy versus psychoeducation, we examined secondary) Tj
T*
(endpoints including anxiety-related functional impairment, depressive symptoms, and) Tj
T*
(perceived distress. At 12 months, the intervention group showed greater reductions in) Tj
T*
(anxiety-related activity disruption \(mean difference 3.2 points on functional impact) Tj
T*
(scale; 95% CI 1.5-4.9; p<0.001\) and depressive symptomatology \(mean difference 1.1 points;) Tj
T*
(95% CI 0.8-1.4; p<0.001\). These differences remained significant at 24 months. Effect) Tj
T*
(sizes for anxiety-related impairment were larger \(Cohen's d=0.48 at 12 months\) than for) Tj
T*
(mood symptoms \(d=0.31\). Approximately 68% of the intervention group achieved clinically) Tj
T*
(significant improvement on at least one secondary measure compared with 41% in the control) Tj
T*
(group. Among multiple anxiety dimensions assessed, social anxiety showed the largest) Tj
T*
(treatment response.) Tj
